<!--
  BlockML VS Code — documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation.ContributionModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:contrib="org.blockml.bml.vscode.contribution"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation"
  xmlns:theme="org.blockml.bml.vscode.theme">

  <name>ContributionModel</name>
  <type>doc:ContributionModel</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to VS Code contributions in BML</is>

  <documentation>
    Contribution → generator mapping:
    • LanguageContribution → contributes.languages + language-configuration.json (comments,
      brackets, autoClosingPairs, surroundingPairs from CharacterPair aggregations). When
      xmlLanguageParticipant is true, also contributes.xmlLanguageParticipants[{ languageId }]
      so vscode-xml keeps applying XSD (xsi:schemaLocation) after .bml is claimed as language bml
    • GrammarContribution → contributes.grammars + syntaxes/*.tmLanguage.json (from structured
      GrammarPattern children, topLevelIncludes, and scopes). When highlightScheme is set,
      framework tag patterns must follow that HighlightScheme's roles/tags/scopes.
    • HighlightScheme / HighlightRole (org.blockml.bml.vscode.theme.*) → SSOT for semantic
      framework-tag coloring; not a package.json contribution by itself — consumed when rendering
      GrammarContribution / tmLanguage
    • IconContribution → contributes.iconThemes + icon theme JSON (themeId / themeLabel /
      themePath) mapping fileExtension / languageId to iconPath
    • ColorThemeContribution → contributes.themes + themes/*.json from theme:ColorTheme
      tokenColors and editor colors (theme:BlockMlDevColorTheme). marketplace=true adds the
      Themes category and emits contributes.themes[].id from ColorTheme.themeId
    • ConfigurationContribution / Setting → contributes.configuration (SSOT for all settings)
    • CommandContribution → contributes.commands
    • KeybindingContribution → contributes.keybindings
    • LanguageServerContribution → vscode-languageclient bootstrap (not a package.json key alone)
    • NavigationContribution → LSP definition/references expectations + optional client providers
    • SemanticHighlightingContribution → semantic token legend / LSP semanticTokens
    • MarketplaceListing → README.md (Marketplace / Open VSX page body). CHANGELOG.md is the
      changelog tab. Distinct from vscode:README (library reading entry).

    Settings must not be invented only in TypeScript — add a Setting under ConfigurationContribution
    first, then generate accessors from BML. Language-config and grammar regexes must not be
    invented only in JSON — amend LanguageContribution / GrammarPattern in BML first. Framework
    tag lists and role scopes must not be invented only in JSON — amend HighlightScheme first, then
    re-render GrammarPatterns + tmLanguage via LLM. Token colors must not be invented only in
    themes/*.json — amend theme:ColorTheme / TokenColorRule in BML first, then re-render.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:GenerationWorkflow" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — BML to generated extension workflow.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:Setting" relation="Defines">
      Individual setting entity.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:ConfigurationContribution" relation="Defines">
      Configuration section holding settings.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:CharacterPair" relation="SeeAlso">
      Bracket / auto-closing pairs for language-configuration.json.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:GrammarPattern" relation="SeeAlso">
      Structured TextMate repository patterns.
    </see>
    <see type="theme:HighlightScheme" relation="SeeAlso">
      Semantic highlight schemes for framework vs domain tags.
    </see>
    <see type="theme:ColorTheme" relation="SeeAlso">
      Editor color theme SSOT (TokenColorRule → themes/*.json).
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:ColorThemeContribution" relation="SeeAlso">
      contributes.themes registration.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:MarketplaceListing" relation="SeeAlso">
      Marketplace README.md listing copy.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:PluginArchitecture" relation="SeeAlso">
      Package and type overview.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
